---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a rule of Flow sends a file to Paperless
    accDescr: Someone uploads, changes, moves, copies or tags a file in Nextcloud. Flow checks the conditions of the rules of the administrators with the operation Send to Paperless, such as the type of the file, a tag of its folder or the group of the user. When a rule matches, Paperless Sync queues the file for its owner with the tags of every matching rule, unless the app is not connected, the file is in the folder of Paperless Sync, has a marker such as [P123] or waits already. With the next run of cron, the background job uploads it as a file sent from Files, with the tags for every import of the inbox and those of the rule, and follows its task. The owner hears of an import that Paperless refused or that failed; one that worked stays in the log. The file stays where it is.

    event["📄 A file is created,<br>changed, moved, copied<br>or gets a tag"]
    rule{"A rule of Flow<br>matches?"}
    check{"Connected, outside<br>the folder of the app,<br>no marker such as<br>[P123], not waiting?"}
    stays["Nothing is sent"]
    queue["Queued for its owner,<br>with the tags of<br>every matching rule"]
    upload{"Upload with the tags<br>of the inbox and<br>of the rule"}
    log["📝 The log: a new<br>document, or one<br>that Paperless had"]
    notified["🔔 A notification to the<br>owner: a refusal or<br>a failed import"]

    event --> rule
    rule -- "no" --> stays
    rule -- "yes" --> check
    check -- "no" --> stays
    check -- "yes" --> queue
    queue -- "next run<br>of cron" --> upload
    upload -- "imported or<br>known" --> log
    upload -- "refused or<br>failed" --> notified

    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    class event,rule,check,stays,queue,log,notified nextcloud
    class upload paperless
